    "engine": "knitr",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"2025 MultiSport Canada Series Champion!\"\ndate: 2026-01-01\ncategories: [notes, series]\nimage: https://storage.googleapis.com/blogs_josa/sport/blog_assets/2025-12-31_MULTISPORT_CANADA_CHAMPIONSHIP/img/thumbnail/IMG_2619.jpg\ndescription: \"A second straight MultiSport Canada series title!\"\ntoc: false\nfreeze: true\ncode-tools: false\nformat:\n  html:\n    toc: false\n    smooth-scroll: true\n    page-layout: full\n    lightbox: true\n---\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n\n\n![MultiSport Canada Champions plaque.](https://storage.googleapis.com/blogs_josa/sport/blog_assets/2025-12-31_MULTISPORT_CANADA_CHAMPIONSHIP/img/thumbnail/IMG_2619.jpg)\n\nBack-to-back.\n\nAfter winning the title in 2024, I managed to defend it in 2025 as well. Last year's win felt like a surprise when I first learned I had topped the series; this time I understood the stakes a little better, which somehow made it both more satisfying and more stressful. If you want the origin story, the first title is in [2024 MultiSport Canada Series Champion!](../2025-01-31_series_champion/index.qmd).\n\n## How the series works\n\nThe MultiSport Canada series pulls together results from races organized by MultiSport Canada across the season. To be eligible for the year-end standings, you need to complete at least three races. At the end of the year, champions are awarded by discipline and category, including sprint triathlon, standard triathlon, sprint duathlon, long-distance events, and others.\n\nThe scoring is simple: the better you place, the more points you earn. The top 10 score on the following scale:\n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<table class=\"table\" style=\"width: auto !important; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\n <thead>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Place </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Points </th>\n  </tr>\n </thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 100 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 2 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 90 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 3 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 85 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 4 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 80 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 5 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 75 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 6 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 70 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 7 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 65 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 8 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 60 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 9 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 55 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 10 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 50 </td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n`````\n:::\n:::\n\n\n\n\nThat structure rewards consistency. Show up, race well, and stack enough results together, and the series starts to tilt in your favor.\n\n## My category: M40-44\n\nHere is the 2025 M40-44 results table:\n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<table class=\"table\" style=\"width: auto !important; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\n <thead>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> Name </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Points </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Races </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Rank </th>\n  </tr>\n </thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> ADRIAN JOSEPH </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 250 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 3 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> HECTOR PALACIOS </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 200 </td>\n   <td style=